lesson: 68
title: Pairs and the one left alone
stars: 0
explain: When things are put in pairs, every pair has 2. An even number makes pairs with none left alone.
explain: An odd number makes pairs with exactly one left alone.
explain: 13 children make 6 pairs, and 1 child is left alone, because 6 + 6 = 12 and 12 + 1 = 13.
vars: a=name n=6..41
answer: (n - n % 2) / 2
exercise: {n} children line up in pairs. How many pairs can they make?
exercise: {a} has {n} socks and puts them in pairs. How many pairs does {a.he} make?
exercise: The teacher puts {n} pupils into pairs for a game. How many full pairs are there?
exercise: {a} has {n} shoes. How many pairs of 2 can {a.he} make?
exercise: {n} ducks swim two by two. How many twos are there?
test: If {n} dancers dance in couples, how many couples dance? (One may have to wait.)
test: {a} matches {n} gloves two at a time. How many matched twos does {a.he} get?
test: How many groups of exactly 2 can be made from {n} people?
exercise: A class in Chicago has {n} pupils. They work in pairs. How many pairs can they form?
exercise: {n} socks hang on the washing line at a house in Leeds. How many pairs of socks can be made from them?
exercise: How many twos are there in {n}?
exercise: {a} puts {n} chairs in rows of two. How many full rows of two are there?
exercise: {n.words} children walk to a park in Toronto two by two. How many full pairs walk together?
exercise: {a} has {n} biscuits and packs them two in a bag. How many full bags does {a.he} make?
exercise: At a dance in Ireland, {n} dancers form couples. How many couples are there?
exercise: Make as many pairs as you can from {n} buttons. How many pairs is that?
test: Two children share each canoe on a lake in Ontario. If {n} children come, how many canoes can be filled with two?
test: {n} shoes are by the door of a house in Sydney. How many complete twos can {a} put together?
test: Out of {n} pupils, how many pairs of partners can a teacher in Cardiff make?
test: {a} puts {n} pencils into packs of two. How many packs of two are full?
test: How many times does 2 fit wholly into {n}?
test: {n} penguins in a New Zealand zoo waddle in twos. How many pairs are there?
exercise: {n} kids, line up in pairs. how many pairs
exercise: {a}'s got {n} socks, pairs em up. how many pairs
exercise: {n+2} — no wait, {n} pupils, teacher puts em in twos. how many full pairs
exercise: Kai reckons {n} kids make {n} pairs. nah, how many pairs really
test: {n} shoes in the hall, how many full pairs can u make
test: dance class has {n} kids, songs 3 mins long. how many couples can dance
test: partners for the trip, {n} of us. how many pairs
exam: Determine the number of complete pairs which may be formed from {n.words} children.
exam: It is given that {a} is in possession of {n} socks. Ascertain the greatest number of complete pairs which {a.he} may assemble therefrom.
exam: A group of {n} pupils is to be arranged in twos. State the number of complete twos which may be so arranged.
exam: Compute the number of pairs obtainable when {n} identical shoes are matched two by two, any shoe remaining unmatched being disregarded.
exercise: At the celebration of life for {a}'s grandad, {n} guests sat two to a table, and anyone left over sat alone. How many tables had two guests?
exercise: {a}'s nan has 'memory problems' and has thrown her {n} socks in one basket. {a} matches them up in pairs. How many full pairs can {a.he} make?
test: {n} kids on the trip, buddy up in 2s, anyone left over goes with sir — usually {a}, 'a strong personality' says {a.his} report, pain in the backside more like. how many pairs
